An absolute `--target` is taken verbatim rather than joined onto the workdir: the file sits outside
the `run` workdir, so joining would miss it and report `not-started`.

`/proc/self/cwd` is how a case names a file it seeded — the sandbox path is generated per run and
cannot be spelled in a `cmd` line.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-run
title: Run
summary: Single-machine fixture for playbook-state.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []
  research: [intake]

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: researching
            when: intake complete
            gates: ["request captured in the artifact"]
          - to: parked
            when: the run is shelved
      researching:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: research complete
      parked: {terminal: true}
      done: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/intake/prompt.md --
---
summary: Intake the request.
---

Intake body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/research/prompt.md --
---
summary: Research the request.
---

Research body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- fixtures/cwd/elsewhere/review.md --
---
status: researching
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping playbook-state fx-run --workdir run --target /proc/self/cwd/elsewhere/review.md
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
playbook: fx-run
workdir: {CWD}/run
states:
  main:
    artifact: /proc/self/cwd/elsewhere/review.md
    status: researching
    next:
    - to: done
      when: research complete
